{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/977619-architecture-of-evil-hives-flesh-edifications-nodes-etc","id":977619,"title":"Architecture of Evil: Hives, Flesh Edifications, Nodes etc..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-27T23:14:20-07:00","id":977619,"title":"Architecture of Evil: Hives, Flesh Edifications, Nodes etc..","content":"So, while i was talking with one of my players. we were discussing the &quot;Aesthetical&quot; differences between the different &quot;Lairs&quot; in the World of Darkness universe.<br /> I think one of the books mentioned that the Nephandi's architecture inspired H.R Giger in general. but how do you imagine this places to look like? (for example) i always felt that the Hives from the BSD look like the Alien Hive in Aliens, resin like wall's and such.<br /> the Nephandi is a bit more abstract (in my opinion). id magine it more like the Hellraiser 2 Laberyth and dissjointed rooms as well as physics.<br /> as for the Spectre hives. i just keep having flashbacks of the american horror story Openings (all of them). old buildings with flickering lights and figures that show up out of nowhere. a rock might look like a skull for a moment, or a branch like an arm trying to reach in...<br /> <br /> as for the Flesh Edification's of the Tzimisces. well, i always thought of &quot;What if the creature from The Thing was a house&quot;, moaning walls. &quot;art&quot; based bodies stacked on top of each other. bones and blood pulsating etc...<br /> <br /> <br /> any thoughts on how you think such places should look like? feel free to mention others that i havent mentioned<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T23:51:52-07:00","id":977638,"title":"","content":"Hellraiser 2 and 3 has a kind of totem pole made of bodies and bits. That's what I imagine Tzimisce furniture is like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-28T03:27:37-07:00","id":977675,"title":"","content":"I just imagined round dirt tunnels for bsd hives of varying sizes (between wolf and multiple crinos). Highly morbid decorations in the larger areas . They're polluted heavily, but are otherwise natural materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 09-28-2016, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-29T16:28:26-07:00","id":978704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/977619-architecture-of-evil-hives-flesh-edifications-nodes-etc#post977619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as for the Flesh Edification's of the Tzimisces. well, i always thought of &quot;What if the creature from The Thing was a house&quot;, moaning walls. &quot;art&quot; based bodies stacked on top of each other. bones and blood pulsating etc...</div> </div> </div> </div><b>The Heart (Montreal): </b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Heart is located in the red light district of Montreal, it serves as the lair of the exotic Widows, it's discreet entrance marked by a small red leather door that seems to pulse in sync with the music inside.<br /> <br /> In the deepest recess of the club is a corridor that leads to a large metallic door, from which moans and the rattling of chains can be heard. On the door itself are two human bodies, a male and a female, fleshcrafted into place.<br /> <br /> The inner sanctum is shaped like a seven pointed star. The walls are made from human flesh and infant bodies, merged together to form one continuous network of skin and veins. A chandelier bathes the room in deep, warm, red light. In each of the seven corners of the inner sanctum is a small shrine dedicated to one of the Seven Deadly Sins - Envy, Gluttony, Greed, Lust, Pride, Sloth and Wrath. These shrines are adorned with living icons that are attached to the living walls. The statues exemplify and constantly perform the sins they represent. The Rose (Tzimisce) and Creamy Jade (Toreador) regard the sanctum as their greatest work of art.<br /> <br /> At the center of the inner sanctum is a dais that's filled with blood. Drops defy gravity by moving from the pool to the ceilings. the blood sustains the room's living walls and shrines.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Golgotha (Egypt):</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In the modern nights, Unre (Harbinger of skulls) makes her haven beneath the swirls sands of Egypt. A vast, sprawling affair, the haven has earned the name Golgotha, as it is festooned with corpses ans <i>zombu </i>in various states of decomposition. Unre conducts grim rituals, vivisections and experiments there, in the deepest bowels of what amounts to a personal underground city, going so far as to trap her rivals' souls in their own bones or ash-heaps after they have met the Final Death so that she may continue to use them.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Temple of eternal whispers (Montreal):</b><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Named for the soft moans and bellows that echo through its halls. Many cholera victims were buried alive after being declared dead by frightened doctors. Those poor souls awoke to discover that their bodies have been sealed into crypts or dumped into a mass grave. their screams echoed through the night, much to the enjoyment of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> - church of the forsaken, the black grove: The shepherds developed a ritual that transformed mortals into distended black trees that moaned in agony.<br /> The nave of the church is crowded by the tortured grove. The trees were once the followers of the infernalists Cedilia and Sangris. Thralls of setite J\u00e9rar and the ghouls of Prince Jonah also stand here. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 09-30-2016, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T12:13:55-07:00","id":980376,"title":"","content":"Yuck. I always like more subtlety with my monsters. For example, if I have someone visiting a Tzimisce, they will find the furniture is formed from living human beings, transformed into useful shapes by their loving mistress. When she is not around, they fornication with abandon, using the specially designed genitalia that she crafted for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T14:08:27-07:00","id":980423,"title":"","content":"Of all of them, I see the Hives of the Black Spirals as the least grotesque. It's still terrifying, but less of the &quot;architecture of flesh and bone&quot; and more carved out of black rock, jagged angles to the labyrinth, green balefire lighting it, carved sigils in the walls, and generally seeming like a burned-out hellscape rather than something Giger-esque. Some may be more or less grotesque depending on the patron, but the general shape seem to be more or less non-Lovecraftian<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Nephandi Labyrinths are a blend of the mundane elements they are built in and the truly grotesque. My standard vision is of an abandoned factory, pipes and machines scattered about, but the closer to the Caul you go, the more the organic elements of the realms beyond the Caul become incorporated into the workings, like mold or moss growing on them or &quot;webs&quot; growing between pieces. Eventually, the entire place becomes covered in the fleshy growth right around the portal of the caul itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}